Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• “disease_code”: identifies cancer type; filter rows where value = 'KIRP'.  
• “clinical_stage”: patient’s clinical stage; must be non‑NULL, group label.  
• “case_barcode”: unique patient ID; join key between the two tables.  
• “project_short_name”: helps double‑check that expression data belong to “TCGA‑KIRP”.  
• “gene_name”: select target genes ‘MT‑CO3’, ‘MT‑CO1’, ‘MT‑CO2’.  
• “HTSeq__FPKM_UQ”: expression value to average / measure distance.  

Typical conditions that will be needed  
• "clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL  
• "disease_code" = 'KIRP'  
• "gene_name" IN ('MT‑CO3','MT‑CO1','MT‑CO2')  
• "project_short_name" = 'TCGA‑KIRP' (extra safeguard)  

Below are 10 exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each returns ≤ 20 rows) that gradually build the information needed for the final analysis.  
All identifiers are wrapped in double quotes and every query ends with LIMIT 20.

```sql
--Description: 1) Look at all distinct disease codes present in the clinical table
SELECT DISTINCT "disease_code"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) List distinct clinical stages specifically for KIRP cases
SELECT DISTINCT "clinical_stage"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"
WHERE "disease_code" = 'KIRP'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Inspect 20 KIRP patients who have a non‑null clinical stage
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "clinical_stage",
       "gender",
       "age_at_diagnosis"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"
WHERE "disease_code" = 'KIRP'
  AND "clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Verify the project names available in the RNA‑seq table
SELECT DISTINCT "project_short_name"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Sample RNA‑seq rows in TCGA‑KIRP for mitochondrial CO genes
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "sample_barcode",
       "gene_name",
       "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-KIRP'
  AND "gene_name" ILIKE 'MT-CO%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Join clinical & expression tables for MT‑CO3 in KIRP
SELECT c."case_barcode",
       c."clinical_stage",
       e."gene_name",
       e."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"  c
JOIN "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION" e
  ON c."case_barcode" = e."case_barcode"
WHERE c."disease_code" = 'KIRP'
  AND c."clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL
  AND e."gene_name" = 'MT-CO3'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Average MT‑CO3 expression by clinical stage (training‑style summary)
SELECT c."clinical_stage",
       AVG(e."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ") AS "avg_MT_CO3_FPKM_UQ"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"  c
JOIN "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION" e
  ON c."case_barcode" = e."case_barcode"
WHERE c."disease_code" = 'KIRP'
  AND c."clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL
  AND e."gene_name" = 'MT-CO3'
GROUP BY c."clinical_stage"
ORDER BY c."clinical_stage"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Pivot: pull all three CO genes per case (one row per patient)
SELECT e."case_barcode",
       MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'MT-CO1' THEN e."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "MT_CO1",
       MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'MT-CO2' THEN e."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "MT_CO2",
       MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'MT-CO3' THEN e."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "MT_CO3"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION" e
WHERE e."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-KIRP'
  AND e."gene_name" IN ('MT-CO1','MT-CO2','MT-CO3')
GROUP BY e."case_barcode"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Compute average of the three genes per clinical stage
WITH expr AS (
  SELECT c."clinical_stage",
         e."case_barcode",
         MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'MT-CO1' THEN e."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "MT_CO1",
         MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'MT-CO2' THEN e."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "MT_CO2",
         MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'MT-CO3' THEN e."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "MT_CO3"
  FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"  c
  JOIN "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION" e
    ON c."case_barcode" = e."case_barcode"
  WHERE c."disease_code" = 'KIRP'
    AND c."clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL
    AND e."gene_name" IN ('MT-CO1','MT-CO2','MT-CO3')
  GROUP BY c."clinical_stage", e."case_barcode"
)
SELECT "clinical_stage",
       AVG("MT_CO1") AS "avg_MT_CO1",
       AVG("MT_CO2") AS "avg_MT_CO2",
       AVG("MT_CO3") AS "avg_MT_CO3"
FROM expr
GROUP BY "clinical_stage"
ORDER BY "clinical_stage"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) (Prototype) Show Euclidean distance from each patient to Stage‑specific mean of the three genes
WITH stage_means AS (
  SELECT "clinical_stage",
         AVG(CASE WHEN "gene_name" = 'MT-CO1' THEN "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "mean_CO1",
         AVG(CASE WHEN "gene_name" = 'MT-CO2' THEN "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "mean_CO2",
         AVG(CASE WHEN "gene_name" = 'MT-CO3' THEN "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "mean_CO3"
  FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"  c
  JOIN "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION" e
    ON c."case_barcode" = e."case_barcode"
  WHERE c."disease_code" = 'KIRP'
    AND c."clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL
    AND e."gene_name" IN ('MT-CO1','MT-CO2','MT-CO3')
  GROUP BY "clinical_stage"
),
patient_expr AS (
  SELECT c."case_barcode",
         MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'MT-CO1' THEN e."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "CO1",
         MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'MT-CO2' THEN e."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "CO2",
         MAX(CASE WHEN e."gene_name" = 'MT-CO3' THEN e."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "CO3"
  FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"  c
  JOIN "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION" e
    ON c."case_barcode" = e."case_barcode"
  WHERE c."disease_code" = 'KIRP'
    AND c."clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL
    AND e."gene_name" IN ('MT-CO1','MT-CO2','MT-CO3')
  GROUP BY c."case_barcode"
)
SELECT p."case_barcode",
       s."clinical_stage",
       SQRT( POWER(p."CO1" - s."mean_CO1", 2) +
             POWER(p."CO2" - s."mean_CO2", 2) +
             POWER(p."CO3" - s."mean_CO3", 2) ) AS "euclidean_distance"
FROM patient_expr p
CROSS JOIN stage_means s
ORDER BY p."case_barcode", "euclidean_distance"
LIMIT 20;
```

These queries progressively examine and prepare the data needed for splitting into train/test, computing stage means, measuring distances, and predicting clinical stage—all while staying within simple SELECT statements.
